WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:17.855
<i>During the Warring States Period,</i>

2
00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:21.587
<i>China was made up of
dozens of nations.</i>

3
00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:24.620
<i>Countless fights between states.</i>

4
00:00:24.913 --> 00:00:26.605
<i>Society was in devastation.</i>

5
00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:36.159
<i>The 7 largest states were known as
Qi, Chu, Yan, Han, Zhao, Wei and Qin.</i>

6
00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.846
<i>The rest was nearly wiped out</i>

7
00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:43.075
<i>a hundred years before the unification.</i>

8
00:00:45.931 --> 00:00:50.266
<i>Qin then conquered Han and Zhao
subsequently.</i>

9
00:01:00.915 --> 00:01:03.478
<i>Year 227 B.C.</i>

10
00:01:03.669 --> 00:01:06.420
<i>When Wei's troops marching towards
the state of Liang.</i>

11
00:01:07.075 --> 00:01:11.409
<i>they were ambushed by Liang
at Mt. Phoenix.</i>

12
00:01:11.785 --> 00:01:13.277
<i>Both sides suffered heavily.</i>

13
00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:18.136
<i>Death toll reached 3,000.</i>

14
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:29.000
Subtitles/Translation: Arigon

15
00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:51.994
Third bro.

16
00:02:55.304 --> 00:02:56.888
Third bro.

17
00:02:58.147 --> 00:03:00.152
You're not lucky as I am.

18
00:03:24.385 --> 00:03:26.318
- General!
- Who are you?

19
00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.233
Liang's soldier.

20
00:05:16.544 --> 00:05:22.723
<i>One main road
leads to homecoming</i>

21
00:05:23.563 --> 00:05:29.772
<i>My home is right at
the foot of Mt. Liang</i>

22
00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:37.389
<i>Soils are rich there
5 acres of farms</i>

23
00:05:37.717 --> 00:05:39.164
Pretty good.

24
00:05:39.353 --> 00:05:45.177
<i>5 acres of farm
What to grow?</i>

25
00:05:52.313 --> 00:05:53.339
Let me tell you something.

26
00:05:53.436 --> 00:05:55.901
When I was a boy, I caught a boar.
My dad had me let go of it.

27
00:05:56.044 --> 00:05:57.730
You know why?

28
00:05:57.874 --> 00:05:59.784
There were other boys
inside that belly.

29
00:05:59.974 --> 00:06:01.700
You have boys?

30
00:06:05.478 --> 00:06:07.007
You know what,

31
00:06:07.908 --> 00:06:09.467
you're my captive now.

32
00:06:13.074 --> 00:06:14.846
You've lost few blood.

33
00:06:15.222 --> 00:06:17.332
Not a big deal.

34
00:06:19.057 --> 00:06:21.295
This is the drug developed
by my family.

35
00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:23.171
Don't spare this to anyone.

36
00:06:27.226 --> 00:06:28.298
You hurt?

37
00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:31.284
Now it gonna hurt more.

38
00:06:33.476 --> 00:06:35.854
You're welcome, young man!

39
00:06:36.135 --> 00:06:38.747
You'll live, you know.

40
00:06:40.193 --> 00:06:41.778
And don't curse.

41
00:06:47.649 --> 00:06:48.966
My dad said,

42
00:06:49.203 --> 00:06:52.824
Scratch when you're itchy,
Smile when you ain't lucky!

43
00:06:56.579 --> 00:06:58.071
Pretty good.

44
00:07:28.112 --> 00:07:29.605
General.

45
00:07:33.539 --> 00:07:34.566
Deputy General Yu.

46
00:07:34.708 --> 00:07:35.876
Yes, I am.

47
00:07:36.158 --> 00:07:37.512
Hang on a sec.

48
00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:40.963
Why you're here?

49
00:07:42.176 --> 00:07:43.529
In pursuit of Liang's.

50
00:07:47.443 --> 00:07:49.495
In pursuit? How many have you killed?

51
00:07:50.441 --> 00:07:51.655
Speak.

52
00:07:52.029 --> 00:07:52.917
One.

53
00:07:53.106 --> 00:07:55.709
- My men must fight hard.
- Liang's came hard on us...

54
00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:57.244
Defend our nation with our lives.

55
00:07:57.387 --> 00:08:01.100
- Please, for the sake of...
- AWOL personnel must face penalty.

56
00:08:01.264 --> 00:08:04.556
General, my company was
all gone last night.

57
00:08:05.469 --> 00:08:08.965
Gone? I was there last night.

58
00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:11.253
In fact, we were ambushed.

59
00:08:11.442 --> 00:08:13.632
And you were the traitor.

60
00:08:25.047 --> 00:08:27.143
You're so cruel.

61
00:08:27.247 --> 00:08:29.628
He saved your life, and you took his.

62
00:08:32.775 --> 00:08:34.801
What you gonna do?

63
00:08:35.688 --> 00:08:36.855
He was right.

64
00:08:37.053 --> 00:08:39.011
You're all dead.

65
00:08:39.295 --> 00:08:40.694
Kill me.

66
00:08:40.883 --> 00:08:42.797
I don't kill POW.

67
00:08:43.635 --> 00:08:47.401
Now, keep begging. I might let
you go, if you tried hard enough.

68
00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.390
Just kill me.

69
00:08:50.809 --> 00:08:52.255
You really want to die?

70
00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.449
Here, let me help you.

71
00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:01.114
Too bad,

72
00:09:02.048 --> 00:09:04.611
I failed my mission.

73
00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:28.693
Want to die?

74
00:09:28.835 --> 00:09:30.888
Die another day.

75
00:09:45.607 --> 00:09:48.497
Prince Wen, we've accomplished.

76
00:09:49.977 --> 00:09:54.323
Like he said, to die with
dignity in a battle field.

77
00:09:54.653 --> 00:09:55.866
You're AWOL.

78
00:09:56.055 --> 00:09:57.967
Not exactly. Just playing dead.

79
00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.070
My dad said, no shame for
living to fight another day,

80
00:10:00.213 --> 00:10:01.472
only for being dead in vain.

81
00:10:01.662 --> 00:10:04.402
Poor Third bro didn't listen to me.
He refused to play dead.

82
00:10:04.551 --> 00:10:05.579
How much am I worth?

83
00:10:05.724 --> 00:10:06.936
It doesn't hurt to tell you.

84
00:10:07.126 --> 00:10:09.316
General alive, 5 acres of farm land.

85
00:10:09.738 --> 00:10:10.812
5 acres.

86
00:10:11.002 --> 00:10:12.355
I have a jade medal in possession.

87
00:10:16.129 --> 00:10:18.136
How much is this broken thingy worth?

88
00:10:18.329 --> 00:10:19.911
A lot.

89
00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.129
I'll keep it as a gift.

90
00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.695
But I don't believe you.

91
00:10:29.759 --> 00:10:31.811
He's one of us. Still alive.

92
00:10:32.837 --> 00:10:35.216
We were ambushed.

93
00:10:46.534 --> 00:10:47.747
Anybody home?

94
00:10:56.085 --> 00:10:57.717
Anybody home?

95
00:11:08.895 --> 00:11:12.339
Someone, bring me meatloaf and liquor!

96
00:11:14.117 --> 00:11:16.541
A big shot like you,
what would you say now?

97
00:11:17.101 --> 00:11:19.793
"Absurd! Take him outside for beheading."

98
00:11:32.055 --> 00:11:33.640
Nothing to eat in here.

99
00:12:07.351 --> 00:12:08.750
General, spare me.

100
00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.644
Liang's archer and infantry unit:
2,000 men in total.

101
00:12:13.835 --> 00:12:15.701
Ambushed our 1,000-strong elite unit.

102
00:12:15.889 --> 00:12:17.755
Both sides were totally wiped out.

103
00:12:17.945 --> 00:12:19.864
This is the sword I gave me.

104
00:12:21.123 --> 00:12:22.570
But where is he now?

105
00:12:22.853 --> 00:12:24.484
I believe we can find me.

106
00:12:25.326 --> 00:12:26.493
Wu,

107
00:12:29.382 --> 00:12:31.955
only if he's still among the living.

108
00:12:36.415 --> 00:12:38.340
War is everywhere now,

109
00:12:39.227 --> 00:12:41.699
where else you can go?

110
00:12:42.724 --> 00:12:44.496
General, have you heard of Shen Shu?

111
00:12:44.686 --> 00:12:47.297
The one in Mt. Phoenix?
A fortunate-telling tree.

112
00:12:49.126 --> 00:12:50.946
Is he your captive?

113
00:12:51.599 --> 00:12:53.697
He's my luck.

114
00:12:54.491 --> 00:12:56.960
Hang in there. We're almost there.

115
00:12:57.152 --> 00:12:58.876
How far?

116
00:12:59.067 --> 00:13:00.501
2 days.

117
00:13:05.973 --> 00:13:06.907
Small potato.

118
00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.263
Don't make me do this.

119
00:13:10.034 --> 00:13:11.155
Don't.

120
00:13:14.567 --> 00:13:16.553
Don't push your luck.

121
00:13:18.857 --> 00:13:20.334
Give me liquor.

122
00:13:20.711 --> 00:13:22.958
- No can do.
- Liquor.

123
00:13:31.477 --> 00:13:33.157
You've fought many battles, haven't you?

124
00:13:33.347 --> 00:13:36.702
Many. You can say
I'm a big time warrior.

125
00:13:37.136 --> 00:13:38.815
Untie me.

126
00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.265
Then you must have killed a lot.

127
00:13:42.409 --> 00:13:43.529
Just too many.

128
00:13:43.719 --> 00:13:46.815
Fought against 8 men at a time.
Like yesterday.

129
00:13:53.223 --> 00:13:55.134
General, would you take me too?

130
00:13:55.326 --> 00:13:57.050
I'd like to become your captive.

131
00:14:00.708 --> 00:14:02.040
Okay.

132
00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:04.932
I know some musical.

133
00:14:05.121 --> 00:14:08.337
General, keep drinking.
I'll entertain you.

134
00:14:14.143 --> 00:14:18.308
- If he turns out to be alive, what then?
- Keep in mind that he's already dead.

135
00:15:09.455 --> 00:15:10.855
Why?

136
00:15:12.765 --> 00:15:16.261
General, you've killed so many.

137
00:15:16.683 --> 00:15:18.874
I'm not a General.

138
00:15:21.763 --> 00:15:24.766
My family were killed by yours.

139
00:15:25.326 --> 00:15:27.377
And I live to sing against my will.

140
00:15:27.521 --> 00:15:29.023
I'm supposed to give you a good time

141
00:15:29.166 --> 00:15:31.172
and serve you, General.

142
00:15:34.064 --> 00:15:36.869
I didn't take pleasure in
drinking with you.

143
00:16:31.051 --> 00:16:32.303
No more fight.

144
00:17:11.278 --> 00:17:14.120
Open the gate. I'm a soldier.

145
00:17:14.267 --> 00:17:16.548
I have taken a Wei's General...

146
00:17:32.103 --> 00:17:33.828
Stop.

147
00:17:38.135 --> 00:17:39.534
Whose this head?

148
00:17:39.699 --> 00:17:41.145
A General of Wei.

149
00:17:47.619 --> 00:17:49.859
That's him. I'm sure.

150
00:17:50.002 --> 00:17:52.519
That's a head of Wei's General.

151
00:17:53.779 --> 00:17:55.131
Reward him.

152
00:17:55.321 --> 00:17:56.860
Just a sec.

153
00:17:57.421 --> 00:17:58.741
Who killed him?

154
00:17:58.884 --> 00:17:59.911
I did.

155
00:18:00.006 --> 00:18:01.642
Really?

156
00:18:02.899 --> 00:18:05.790
He must be an AWOL.
Cut off a head from a dead man.

157
00:18:07.712 --> 00:18:08.830
Behead him.

158
00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.144
That's not true!

159
00:19:05.497 --> 00:19:07.702
You gonna have to kill me
if you don't let me go.

160
00:19:07.847 --> 00:19:09.664
Or I'll kill you in a heart beat.

161
00:19:10.598 --> 00:19:12.091
Kill, kill, kill.

162
00:19:12.292 --> 00:19:13.599
I grow farms.

163
00:19:13.788 --> 00:19:16.444
I don't kill and I don't want to kill.

164
00:19:16.588 --> 00:19:18.360
You're getting me mad.

165
00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.507
I'm not gonna kill you.

166
00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:22.796
Can't believe I just got
fooled by some woman.

167
00:19:23.962 --> 00:19:27.008
I gave her food to each,
and she gave me pill to swallow.

168
00:19:27.655 --> 00:19:30.745
You deceived her first,
so it sounds fair.

169
00:19:31.851 --> 00:19:34.088
She should have hit you instead.

170
00:19:34.371 --> 00:19:36.003
Stupid helmet.

171
00:19:38.985 --> 00:19:41.362
What did she say to you last night?

172
00:19:44.073 --> 00:19:45.485
You small potato.

173
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.615
Who's stronger, me or him?

174
00:19:54.709 --> 00:19:55.750
He's a natural.

175
00:19:55.891 --> 00:19:58.228
- So I'm nowhere to compete with him?
- You're too soft and he got the heart.

176
00:19:58.467 --> 00:20:00.270
To become the King,

177
00:20:02.867 --> 00:20:04.830
you must learn from him.

178
00:20:05.085 --> 00:20:07.714
I'll take a unit and head for Liang's.
Why don't you go back...

179
00:20:07.803 --> 00:20:10.227
I won't go back until I see him.

180
00:20:10.881 --> 00:20:12.095
You know what,

181
00:20:12.424 --> 00:20:14.336
I've been looking forward to

182
00:20:14.572 --> 00:20:18.112
life of peace and farms to grow
for 20 years.

183
00:20:47.674 --> 00:20:50.697
The wagon is not here.
The rope was cut off.

184
00:21:20.568 --> 00:21:23.147
Stop playing dead.
I'm too smart for that.

185
00:21:50.764 --> 00:21:52.500
We better stay away from the main road.

186
00:21:52.690 --> 00:21:54.183
Let's take a detour.

187
00:21:54.382 --> 00:21:55.829
Like this track.

188
00:21:56.018 --> 00:21:58.312
Just don't lose the map.

189
00:22:02.645 --> 00:22:04.650
Strong liquor. Must be Liang's.

190
00:22:07.306 --> 00:22:11.919
<i>One small track
leads the way to home.</i>

191
00:22:20.350 --> 00:22:22.046
What now?

192
00:22:24.153 --> 00:22:28.533
Like my dad said, step in shit.
Something good awaits me.

193
00:22:29.002 --> 00:22:30.355
It's an ambush.

194
00:22:30.544 --> 00:22:32.101
I get it.

195
00:22:37.766 --> 00:22:40.795
What's loaded on that wagon?

196
00:22:40.986 --> 00:22:41.826
Nothing particular.

197
00:22:41.969 --> 00:22:43.229
Rip him.

198
00:22:44.313 --> 00:22:45.619
Rip him off!

199
00:22:49.709 --> 00:22:52.038
- Wait, wait...
- Who are you?

200
00:22:52.276 --> 00:22:53.815
A General.

201
00:22:55.911 --> 00:22:58.056
Says you.

202
00:22:59.549 --> 00:23:01.273
Beat him.

203
00:23:01.787 --> 00:23:03.654
Beat him down.

204
00:23:03.797 --> 00:23:05.754
Stop!

205
00:23:09.786 --> 00:23:11.208
Stop! Stop!

206
00:23:12.746 --> 00:23:13.728
Sorry.

207
00:23:17.457 --> 00:23:18.810
Please... stop.

208
00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:21.648
Take whatever you want,
just let us go.

209
00:23:22.585 --> 00:23:24.719
What possibly do you have,
besides this piece of junk?

210
00:23:24.839 --> 00:23:25.719
I want revenge!

211
00:23:25.862 --> 00:23:27.541
Shut your mouth!

212
00:23:28.288 --> 00:23:30.525
Who's this guy?

213
00:23:31.134 --> 00:23:32.541
He?

214
00:23:32.776 --> 00:23:34.316
He... he's my son.

215
00:23:34.506 --> 00:23:35.643
No! I'm not his son...

216
00:23:35.833 --> 00:23:37.221
You little prick!

217
00:23:39.807 --> 00:23:42.436
He's crazy. He thinks he's going to war.
I'm taking him back to grow farms.

218
00:23:42.549 --> 00:23:44.462
Grow farms? There's nothing left
to grow because of the wars.

219
00:23:44.651 --> 00:23:46.452
- Revenge!
- Get lost!

220
00:23:46.597 --> 00:23:49.467
I'm in charge here.
I say we take the wagon.

221
00:23:49.666 --> 00:23:51.066
Unfaithful prick!

222
00:23:54.002 --> 00:23:56.792
You got a death wish?
This helmet will get you killed.

223
00:23:56.882 --> 00:23:59.876
- How about this?
- This? Will you ever learn?

224
00:23:59.935 --> 00:24:01.938
Let's go!

225
00:24:17.541 --> 00:24:19.127
Bunch of fools.

226
00:24:19.985 --> 00:24:22.343
They had no idea you're the MVP
"Most Valuable Package" here.

227
00:24:25.046 --> 00:24:26.818
Your son?

228
00:24:27.009 --> 00:24:28.453
I'm gonna treat you good!

229
00:24:28.645 --> 00:24:33.907
So tie me up and
take me back to your farms!

230
00:24:48.395 --> 00:24:50.945
Don't move. Don't breathe.

231
00:25:26.440 --> 00:25:28.176
You were trying to strangle me to death?

232
00:25:30.145 --> 00:25:32.195
If it wasn't me...

233
00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:47.221
Prick!

234
00:26:02.195 --> 00:26:04.000
It's not Dim Mak.

235
00:26:04.328 --> 00:26:07.498
My dad was right.
I stepped in shit.

236
00:26:10.490 --> 00:26:11.748
Pretty good.

237
00:26:16.673 --> 00:26:18.505
Don't hurt us. I'm begging you!

238
00:26:29.818 --> 00:26:31.219
Hold it there.

239
00:26:39.322 --> 00:26:42.957
I could kill him,
or I could spare him.

240
00:26:43.239 --> 00:26:45.010
I just have the power.

241
00:26:48.458 --> 00:26:52.138
1 acre for growing beans.
1 acre for melons.

242
00:26:52.886 --> 00:26:56.800
How about 2 acres for beans,
2 acres for white grains?

243
00:26:57.207 --> 00:27:00.017
No! 3 acres for beans.

244
00:27:10.282 --> 00:27:11.790
Tell me,

245
00:27:12.402 --> 00:27:15.480
what I should do with
5 acres of farmland?

246
00:27:15.670 --> 00:27:17.035
I can offer you a thousand acres.

247
00:27:17.225 --> 00:27:18.538
That's too much.

248
00:27:18.729 --> 00:27:21.526
I couldn't handle that much.

249
00:27:23.343 --> 00:27:27.072
White grain or bean, what to grow?

250
00:27:27.261 --> 00:27:30.617
I'd say rice. I love rice.

251
00:27:31.364 --> 00:27:35.001
White grain and rice are
the same thing, fool!

252
00:27:36.399 --> 00:27:37.948
You tired?

253
00:27:38.274 --> 00:27:40.093
Feeling comfy, right?

254
00:27:51.816 --> 00:27:53.309
Now I'm relieved.

255
00:27:53.778 --> 00:27:56.493
5 acres, I'd work my butt off.

256
00:27:57.426 --> 00:27:59.663
Right, I'll need some buffalo.

257
00:27:59.991 --> 00:28:03.149
One male, one female.

258
00:28:03.386 --> 00:28:06.320
The male will work in the farms.
The female will give milk.

259
00:28:06.410 --> 00:28:08.816
I'm dying to know how you're gonna
drag me all the way to Liang's.

260
00:28:08.959 --> 00:28:10.152
Wait, I can't milk a cow.

261
00:28:11.601 --> 00:28:13.912
So I'll need a wife who can do that.

262
00:28:17.518 --> 00:28:19.476
My eldest brother was a great warrior.

263
00:28:19.990 --> 00:28:21.344
He fought till death.

264
00:28:22.511 --> 00:28:25.027
My second brother was a honest person.

265
00:28:25.672 --> 00:28:26.885
He died on the battlefield as well.

266
00:28:29.215 --> 00:28:32.709
I'm the last seed of the family.

267
00:28:33.690 --> 00:28:36.720
General, do you have any siblings?

268
00:28:38.025 --> 00:28:39.611
Wish I hadn't.

269
00:28:52.309 --> 00:28:53.909
Why are you taking me here?

270
00:28:55.495 --> 00:28:57.408
I couldn't find 'em.

271
00:28:57.596 --> 00:29:00.431
The Mt. Phoenix is huge!
There's a lot of grounds to cover...

272
00:29:00.526 --> 00:29:01.927
Was he being tied up?

273
00:29:02.118 --> 00:29:05.892
Yes, his dad tied him up.
Said he's crazy or something...

274
00:29:06.080 --> 00:29:09.622
They both appeared to be crazy...

275
00:29:10.555 --> 00:29:12.015
Can I go back now?

276
00:29:31.663 --> 00:29:33.996
Revenge...

277
00:29:44.196 --> 00:29:48.901
They want to take you back from me?
It's not gonna be easy.

278
00:29:49.975 --> 00:29:51.653
I've been in battles for years,

279
00:29:52.308 --> 00:29:55.663
never seen an
elegant arrow like this one.

280
00:29:56.643 --> 00:29:59.905
I've seen this.
It's someone not friendly.

281
00:30:01.956 --> 00:30:05.125
People like you just asking this
for yourself.

282
00:30:05.965 --> 00:30:09.600
You know, they have you
and you'll die.

283
00:30:10.161 --> 00:30:12.584
I have you and you'll live.

284
00:30:12.821 --> 00:30:14.453
You are right.

285
00:30:14.782 --> 00:30:16.506
I don't want to die in vain.

286
00:30:18.325 --> 00:30:19.444
I'll come with you.

287
00:30:23.653 --> 00:30:25.342
Turns out General is afraid of death.

288
00:30:25.718 --> 00:30:27.396
If I die, I'll die with dignity.

289
00:30:39.177 --> 00:30:40.913
This way, or that way?

290
00:30:41.288 --> 00:30:44.605
Even if we make it to Liang's,
I could make a truce

291
00:30:44.795 --> 00:30:46.381
with one condition: your execution.

292
00:30:46.570 --> 00:30:48.927
Don't fool me.
Nobody fools me.

293
00:30:49.089 --> 00:30:51.374
Except that woman who drugged you.

294
00:30:51.606 --> 00:30:52.959
You have lots of women?

295
00:30:54.094 --> 00:30:57.681
Let's talk about you.
What type of women you like?

296
00:30:58.802 --> 00:31:00.408
We have the lustful,

297
00:31:01.972 --> 00:31:03.958
and the educated.

298
00:31:04.491 --> 00:31:06.216
I like the honest ones.

299
00:31:07.242 --> 00:31:10.690
But I'd probably take the educated.
She could teach me how to read.

300
00:31:19.306 --> 00:31:20.751
You don't have a woman, right?

301
00:31:24.057 --> 00:31:25.737
That woman, what did she say to you?

302
00:31:25.972 --> 00:31:29.346
I'll tell you, if you can make it
back to Liang's.

303
00:31:29.794 --> 00:31:31.202
You guys, go down there.

304
00:31:31.390 --> 00:31:33.535
Back to where we came.
Keep a lookout.

305
00:31:46.689 --> 00:31:48.274
Who is that?

306
00:31:49.302 --> 00:31:52.749
The Others.
They're bound to their own rules.

307
00:31:53.636 --> 00:31:55.175
Go make your acquaintance.

308
00:31:55.364 --> 00:31:56.437
They don't speak our language.

309
00:31:56.581 --> 00:31:58.770
They are passionate people.
Good fighters too.

310
00:31:59.145 --> 00:32:00.638
Better stay away from 'em.

311
00:32:07.204 --> 00:32:09.068
Hurry up, you don't look that tired.

312
00:32:11.503 --> 00:32:14.030
Birds are gathering around,

313
00:32:14.203 --> 00:32:17.230
but Phoenixes don't go with the flow.

314
00:32:18.257 --> 00:32:21.518
What chicken and ducks
are you talking about?

315
00:32:22.172 --> 00:32:25.706
If a phoenix lost its fur,
it'd make a chicken look elegant.

316
00:32:31.396 --> 00:32:33.428
You're good at throwing rocks.

317
00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:36.792
I used to hunt wild chicken
with rocks when I was a boy.

318
00:32:37.849 --> 00:32:38.749
Hey.

319
00:32:38.950 --> 00:32:41.373
You know why our troops camped
at the Mt. Phoenix?

320
00:32:41.516 --> 00:32:42.729
How would I know?

321
00:32:42.919 --> 00:32:46.269
Nevertheless, we had hidden there
for 2 days waiting for you.

322
00:32:47.347 --> 00:32:49.518
That's what I thought, a set up.

323
00:32:49.958 --> 00:32:51.589
If it wasn't an ambush,

324
00:32:51.779 --> 00:32:55.003
my elite unit would have
crushed you majorly

325
00:32:55.309 --> 00:32:58.003
and conquered Liang.

326
00:32:59.608 --> 00:33:03.288
Stop the nonsense.
We are not that weak.

327
00:33:04.036 --> 00:33:07.986
Anyway, an AWOL like you,
it's a shame to Liang.

328
00:33:26.250 --> 00:33:29.046
Now, see how you elite you are.

329
00:33:32.718 --> 00:33:35.096
General versus AWOL private?

330
00:33:37.299 --> 00:33:39.816
Liang versus Wei. Fair and simple.

331
00:33:40.329 --> 00:33:43.478
You want fair?
Keep your hands off my wound.

332
00:33:45.184 --> 00:33:46.862
You have your wish.

333
00:34:37.514 --> 00:34:38.819
You're dead.

334
00:34:41.335 --> 00:34:43.106
You're dead too.
We're both dead.

335
00:34:43.213 --> 00:34:44.380
Pervert.

336
00:34:55.624 --> 00:34:57.862
War is over. Wei won.

337
00:35:19.744 --> 00:35:22.678
Wars have been around these years.
More people have joined the military.

338
00:35:22.821 --> 00:35:24.221
He kills him, and he gets killed by him.

339
00:35:24.411 --> 00:35:25.764
What's the attraction?

340
00:35:27.814 --> 00:35:30.516
Liang wins. Liang wins.

341
00:35:31.682 --> 00:35:33.462
You call this fair?

342
00:35:34.116 --> 00:35:36.667
It's war.
No such thing as being fair.

343
00:35:47.387 --> 00:35:51.188
We'll soon have meat to eat.
Now, have some appetizer.

344
00:35:59.031 --> 00:36:00.477
Lost your appetite?

345
00:36:02.210 --> 00:36:03.701
Fine by me.

346
00:36:10.035 --> 00:36:13.482
General, what do you eat when
there is no war to go to?

347
00:36:16.138 --> 00:36:18.980
Meat and seafood.

348
00:36:19.680 --> 00:36:22.663
Any good food you can
possibly think of.

349
00:36:23.325 --> 00:36:25.409
Now I get it.
You people constantly go to war

350
00:36:25.505 --> 00:36:27.509
just because of digestion problems.

351
00:36:30.125 --> 00:36:31.756
Didn't you say you can't read?

352
00:36:35.111 --> 00:36:38.978
My dad taught me these 2 words.
They are the easiest to write.

353
00:36:42.051 --> 00:36:45.577
These 2 words are not easy
to write at all.

354
00:36:46.302 --> 00:36:47.841
Why don't you go to Wei with me.

355
00:36:48.729 --> 00:36:50.314
I can offer you a high position.

356
00:36:50.503 --> 00:36:51.669
I forgot to tell you one thing.

357
00:36:51.860 --> 00:36:55.500
General alive, the rewards will be farmland
and money. No more serving in military.

358
00:36:55.682 --> 00:36:58.300
There will be no more killing for me.
Just me and the farms.

359
00:36:58.489 --> 00:37:00.999
When there's a war, there's a winner.

360
00:37:01.419 --> 00:37:05.146
A winner of unification of China.
Only that will put an end to wars.

361
00:37:05.383 --> 00:37:08.318
Only that will give you little people
a normal life.

362
00:37:08.507 --> 00:37:09.497
You know what,

363
00:37:09.686 --> 00:37:11.406
we could have
lived our normal life,

364
00:37:11.597 --> 00:37:13.692
if you had just left us alone!

365
00:37:17.565 --> 00:37:18.730
You really don't want a bite?

366
00:37:18.884 --> 00:37:22.154
Frankly, I'm a bit hungry.

367
00:37:53.174 --> 00:37:54.573
Here comes our meat!

368
00:37:55.601 --> 00:37:57.465
Wonderful meat.

369
00:38:03.006 --> 00:38:04.731
I'll get you firewood.

370
00:38:05.713 --> 00:38:08.006
You have babies. Can't eat you.

371
00:38:08.799 --> 00:38:10.153
My dad said...

372
00:38:15.228 --> 00:38:16.487
Let's go. Let's go!

373
00:38:17.048 --> 00:38:18.726
Someone is coming. Let's go!

374
00:38:18.869 --> 00:38:21.524
Why the panic? He's alone.

375
00:38:45.550 --> 00:38:47.041
It's our guy.

376
00:38:50.907 --> 00:38:52.678
Hey, bro.

377
00:38:58.780 --> 00:38:59.983
Bastard!

378
00:39:22.911 --> 00:39:25.021
<i>You. Go that way.</i>

379
00:39:44.328 --> 00:39:46.859
A Liang-made sword.

380
00:40:10.695 --> 00:40:11.908
On your Knees.

381
00:40:13.028 --> 00:40:16.067
I'm a Liang's soldier.
I only knee to Liang's superiors.

382
00:40:20.844 --> 00:40:23.001
- Now what?
- You are a scout from Liang's.

383
00:40:23.195 --> 00:40:24.005
Yes.

384
00:40:24.100 --> 00:40:25.609
- What about you?
- I'm a scout too.

385
00:40:25.749 --> 00:40:26.636
What are you scouting for?

386
00:40:26.779 --> 00:40:28.132
I'm going to the battlefield
at Mt. Phoenix. No...

387
00:40:28.227 --> 00:40:29.813
No survivors found.

388
00:40:29.932 --> 00:40:31.237
Why take the track?

389
00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:32.593
Your convoy is taking the main road...

390
00:40:32.734 --> 00:40:34.229
Track is faster...

391
00:40:34.372 --> 00:40:35.863
Pretty fast.

392
00:40:36.007 --> 00:40:37.228
I don't know him.

393
00:40:37.418 --> 00:40:38.625
What?

394
00:40:39.008 --> 00:40:41.345
He's got lightheaded
after falling off from a horse.

395
00:40:41.524 --> 00:40:43.391
No... Yes, I fell...

396
00:40:43.581 --> 00:40:46.640
- Either way I don't know you.
- What?

397
00:40:46.816 --> 00:40:49.193
You don't kill scouts.
That's agreement during wars.

398
00:40:49.336 --> 00:40:50.722
Is this your sword?

399
00:40:50.964 --> 00:40:51.765
Yes.

400
00:40:51.907 --> 00:40:53.820
Why you're carrying
a General type sword?

401
00:40:54.057 --> 00:40:55.315
I borrowed it...

402
00:40:55.458 --> 00:40:56.818
You're not a scout.

403
00:40:59.415 --> 00:41:00.315
No, I'm not.

404
00:41:00.459 --> 00:41:01.822
Where is the Wei's General?

405
00:41:02.023 --> 00:41:03.235
I don't know.

406
00:41:03.426 --> 00:41:04.777
Don't you lie to me!

407
00:41:05.758 --> 00:41:07.203
I know, I know.

408
00:41:07.903 --> 00:41:09.815
I've got your General.

409
00:41:10.005 --> 00:41:11.264
You got balls.

410
00:41:13.780 --> 00:41:15.809
- I got no balls!
- Where is he?

411
00:41:15.992 --> 00:41:17.809
- He's fled.
- You're no use to us then.

412
00:41:17.966 --> 00:41:19.925
No. No. I-I hid him.

413
00:41:20.078 --> 00:41:21.152
Take us there.

414
00:41:21.341 --> 00:41:23.628
- He's really gone.
- Are you messing with me?

415
00:41:28.196 --> 00:41:31.364
Back off! You all back off!

416
00:41:31.506 --> 00:41:33.278
Back off!

417
00:41:43.988 --> 00:41:44.921
Stay back!

418
00:41:45.016 --> 00:41:47.915
- If I die, you won't get anything.
- What do you want?

419
00:41:50.102 --> 00:41:51.500
Rewards.

420
00:41:52.155 --> 00:41:53.741
I can give you that.

421
00:41:54.022 --> 00:41:55.793
Shame on you.

422
00:42:00.218 --> 00:42:03.155
One of you is useless to me.

423
00:42:23.595 --> 00:42:25.694
Now what?

424
00:42:30.119 --> 00:42:31.890
Get him!

425
00:43:30.969 --> 00:43:32.461
Pardon me.

426
00:43:34.559 --> 00:43:36.190
Wu.

427
00:43:39.218 --> 00:43:40.525
Stand down.

428
00:43:43.242 --> 00:43:44.781
Let them through.

429
00:44:13.284 --> 00:44:15.903
He's still alive, isn't he?

430
00:44:54.543 --> 00:44:55.849
Pretty good.

431
00:44:56.224 --> 00:44:59.019
Just a General, not a big deal.

432
00:44:59.999 --> 00:45:03.022
Maybe I'd capture their King later.

433
00:45:05.171 --> 00:45:07.252
Am I really a shame to Liang?

434
00:45:08.583 --> 00:45:10.127
Am I?

435
00:45:22.786 --> 00:45:23.998
Come on.

436
00:45:25.025 --> 00:45:28.007
Come get me!

437
00:45:31.873 --> 00:45:34.200
I'm not dead yet.

438
00:45:34.603 --> 00:45:36.810
<i>Didn't expect that, right?</i>

439
00:45:37.231 --> 00:45:41.407
<i>Because of your conspiracy,
1,000 brave men got killed.</i>

440
00:45:41.945 --> 00:45:45.345
<i>They'll haunt you
for the rest of your life!</i>

441
00:45:46.325 --> 00:45:47.769
And you.

442
00:45:48.725 --> 00:45:51.287
A pity man.

443
00:45:51.848 --> 00:45:54.608
<i>A dishonorable AWOL.</i>

444
00:45:55.401 --> 00:45:57.778
One main road leads the way
to homecoming

445
00:45:57.966 --> 00:46:00.949
empty-handed!

446
00:46:13.845 --> 00:46:15.896
Where you come from?

447
00:46:17.062 --> 00:46:18.740
Where's your home?

448
00:46:19.441 --> 00:46:21.305
When I fulfill the conquest

449
00:46:21.495 --> 00:46:24.523
I'll start building my big boat.

450
00:46:24.946 --> 00:46:28.307
Yeah. I'm gonna sail off
on the night of the full moon

451
00:46:28.589 --> 00:46:30.593
and travel the whole world.

452
00:46:30.969 --> 00:46:32.507
My father said,

453
00:46:32.975 --> 00:46:36.748
paint a dragon on the ship,
and it'll attract a phoenix.

454
00:46:36.938 --> 00:46:39.640
The day you the Prince are crowned,
you will get anything you want.

455
00:46:39.783 --> 00:46:43.870
To become a King, me and him
we'd never be the same like before.

456
00:46:44.024 --> 00:46:46.029
Take some rest, Prince.

457
00:46:48.033 --> 00:46:51.600
My dad said, a sparrow could
one day become a phoenix.

458
00:46:52.832 --> 00:46:54.324
Pretty good.

459
00:47:42.786 --> 00:47:44.055
Why did you trick me?

460
00:47:44.247 --> 00:47:45.599
I wanted to hit you.

461
00:47:45.741 --> 00:47:47.234
So kill me, General.

462
00:47:48.213 --> 00:47:50.171
I'm not a General.
I'm a private.

463
00:47:50.408 --> 00:47:53.342
What's the difference?
You just kill.

464
00:47:55.439 --> 00:47:57.722
Hey, you're lost, right?

465
00:47:57.921 --> 00:48:01.522
You really think that when you get to
Shen Shu, everything will be all right?

466
00:48:05.188 --> 00:48:06.960
I'm a small potato.

467
00:48:12.224 --> 00:48:13.865
This map I have here,

468
00:48:14.577 --> 00:48:16.546
will get you to Shen Shu.

469
00:48:19.295 --> 00:48:22.358
You'll get a lot of grounds to cover.
Take this horse with you.

470
00:48:28.377 --> 00:48:30.008
I give this back to you.

471
00:48:51.052 --> 00:48:53.383
You're hungry? Me too.

472
00:48:54.373 --> 00:48:56.189
Need to find something to eat.

473
00:49:18.037 --> 00:49:21.803
<i>At the bottom of the mountain.
Soils are rich.</i>

474
00:49:22.007 --> 00:49:25.183
<i>5 acres of farmland</i>

475
00:49:26.628 --> 00:49:30.803
<i>5 acres of fine land</i>

476
00:49:31.508 --> 00:49:34.773
<i>What to grow?</i>

477
00:49:34.822 --> 00:49:35.990
- You're wrong.
- You're wrong.

478
00:49:36.133 --> 00:49:37.812
Stop arguing.

479
00:49:38.048 --> 00:49:42.983
If you want to be a successful diplomat,
you just don't one thing.

480
00:49:43.187 --> 00:49:44.166
What's that?

481
00:49:44.356 --> 00:49:45.289
Patience.

482
00:49:45.479 --> 00:49:46.413
Mister,

483
00:49:46.556 --> 00:49:48.327
please tell me which way is Wei.

484
00:49:48.622 --> 00:49:53.415
- That way.
- No, that way.

485
00:49:53.810 --> 00:49:57.210
<i>Wei has geographical advantages,
with Liang acting like a front shield,</i>

486
00:49:57.354 --> 00:49:59.777
<i>and Chu like a shield on the back.</i>

487
00:50:02.014 --> 00:50:04.353
<i>You can run, but you can't hide.</i>

488
00:50:41.320 --> 00:50:43.011
This is your new home now.

489
00:50:43.930 --> 00:50:45.516
I'm going home too.

490
00:50:49.940 --> 00:50:51.897
You live a good life.

491
00:50:55.717 --> 00:50:57.489
Pretty good.

492
00:52:39.765 --> 00:52:45.353
<i>One main road
leads to homecoming</i>

493
00:52:46.750 --> 00:52:50.942
<i>My home is right at
the foot of Mt. Liang</i>

494
00:52:51.969 --> 00:52:54.484
<i>Soils are rich there...</i>

495
00:52:57.561 --> 00:52:58.869
Pretty good.

496
00:53:01.383 --> 00:53:02.642
Pretty good.

497
00:53:10.819 --> 00:53:12.471
Easy, easy.

498
00:53:15.545 --> 00:53:17.783
I should have killed you in that inn.

499
00:53:17.972 --> 00:53:20.627
I should have let you
be the black bear's lunch.

500
00:53:22.213 --> 00:53:24.728
Don't get too tight, you understand me?

501
00:53:25.488 --> 00:53:26.793
They're taking us to a tomb.

502
00:53:26.983 --> 00:53:28.242
Tomb?

503
00:53:28.432 --> 00:53:30.552
- Get us buried in mass grave.
- Buried?

504
00:53:42.734 --> 00:53:44.645
How far is Liang from here?

505
00:53:44.788 --> 00:53:47.257
1 day if you take the river.

506
00:53:47.541 --> 00:53:49.126
What village you come from?

507
00:53:49.327 --> 00:53:50.632
Three Legs Cave.

508
00:53:50.824 --> 00:53:53.431
Looks like your plan isn't going well.

509
00:53:54.458 --> 00:53:56.882
We'll see. You're still my captive.

510
00:53:57.071 --> 00:53:59.680
Hey, I'm not your captive.

511
00:53:59.870 --> 00:54:01.919
I'm his captive.

512
00:55:31.543 --> 00:55:33.964
Trade him with a horse.

513
00:55:41.788 --> 00:55:43.373
Prince, look out!

514
00:56:02.833 --> 00:56:04.091
Line up.

515
00:56:36.309 --> 00:56:38.781
- How to take this thing off?
- I'm about to ask you the same question.

516
00:56:57.873 --> 00:56:59.273
Wu!

517
00:57:42.995 --> 00:57:44.255
I have an idea.

518
00:57:44.399 --> 00:57:45.285
Just say it.

519
00:57:45.475 --> 00:57:47.479
Remember, we're in the same boat.

520
00:57:48.598 --> 00:57:50.556
Yes, like my dad said,

521
00:57:50.745 --> 00:57:53.476
Whether it's a an eagle or a chicken,
they are just meat once placed in a hotpot.

522
00:57:53.966 --> 00:57:55.083
Figured.

523
00:58:32.748 --> 00:58:34.055
Need help.

524
00:58:34.290 --> 00:58:36.210
Not a perfect idea...

525
00:58:39.511 --> 00:58:41.511
but still a good plan.

526
00:58:49.152 --> 00:58:50.652
Come on.

527
00:59:15.953 --> 00:59:18.072
- Wu.
- Yes.

528
00:59:21.456 --> 00:59:22.948
You finally fight me with a real sword.

529
00:59:23.137 --> 00:59:25.932
Sorry, you're no longer my master now.

530
00:59:42.400 --> 00:59:45.675
What a pity,
you're my best student ever.

531
00:59:57.735 --> 00:59:58.900
Get on it.

532
01:00:01.649 --> 01:00:03.141
Buffalo, faster.

533
01:00:37.276 --> 01:00:39.161
Prince, make your way out.

534
01:01:30.881 --> 01:01:34.253
- This way.
- That way.

535
01:01:35.782 --> 01:01:39.088
Hey, you know what,
I didn't want to save you.

536
01:01:39.648 --> 01:01:41.977
This buffalo just lost his temper.

537
01:01:44.493 --> 01:01:46.497
Was this buffalo too power

538
01:01:46.486 --> 01:01:48.319
or the wall was too weak?

539
01:01:48.462 --> 01:01:50.978
Not matter what, thank you.

540
01:01:51.260 --> 01:01:52.985
Pretty good.

541
01:01:54.384 --> 01:01:55.504
What's with your waist belt?

542
01:01:57.322 --> 01:01:58.534
My secret.

543
01:01:58.725 --> 01:02:01.240
Before we go separate ways,
I'll have a secret to tell.

544
01:02:02.639 --> 01:02:04.597
You want to know why those people
wanted to capture me?

545
01:02:04.748 --> 01:02:05.869
No, I don't want to know.

546
01:02:06.059 --> 01:02:08.435
People like you are so complicated.

547
01:02:08.579 --> 01:02:11.327
Since the day we met,
everything has become complicated.

548
01:02:12.555 --> 01:02:13.926
Small potato.

549
01:02:14.680 --> 01:02:15.798
You're still my POW.

550
01:02:15.999 --> 01:02:17.632
Can't let you walk out on me!

551
01:02:20.147 --> 01:02:22.684
- You've delayed my business.
- You're my business.

552
01:02:26.546 --> 01:02:28.412
I know, I'm your farmland.

553
01:02:28.601 --> 01:02:31.443
Yes, 5 acres of it.

554
01:02:31.692 --> 01:02:33.509
And the reward money.

555
01:02:33.653 --> 01:02:35.983
Yes, a pocketful of it.

556
01:02:38.405 --> 01:02:39.805
- Stop!
- Why?

557
01:02:39.905 --> 01:02:42.844
- I'm ordering you!
- You can't trick me!

558
01:02:43.040 --> 01:02:44.739
Thanks for the warning...

559
01:03:05.996 --> 01:03:07.266
This can't hold any longer.

560
01:03:07.873 --> 01:03:08.947
Get off of my back.

561
01:03:09.090 --> 01:03:10.163
Not a chance.

562
01:03:10.352 --> 01:03:11.997
I'll grab you after you let go of me.

563
01:03:12.034 --> 01:03:13.804
You think I'm that stupid?

564
01:03:14.366 --> 01:03:15.625
Let's find out.

565
01:03:31.825 --> 01:03:33.223
Wu.

566
01:03:34.948 --> 01:03:36.394
Prince.

567
01:03:38.538 --> 01:03:39.935
Why?

568
01:03:40.730 --> 01:03:45.759
He's still alive. Is that fate?

569
01:03:45.903 --> 01:03:47.683
Prince, let's head back to Wei.

570
01:03:47.873 --> 01:03:50.668
No! You don't how I feel.

571
01:04:11.382 --> 01:04:13.441
You really are some piece of work.

572
01:04:17.345 --> 01:04:20.605
Go ahead. Tie me up.

573
01:04:21.677 --> 01:04:23.410
Just take a look around.

574
01:04:25.322 --> 01:04:27.353
Take a look around at this hell hole!

575
01:04:38.218 --> 01:04:39.618
Where are we?

576
01:04:51.448 --> 01:04:55.041
Save your breath.
We're gonna die down here.

577
01:05:03.227 --> 01:05:09.466
<i>One main leads
to homecoming</i>

578
01:05:10.493 --> 01:05:16.341
<i>My home is right at
the foot of Mt. Liang</i>

579
01:05:17.851 --> 01:05:20.645
<i>Soils are rich there</i>

580
01:05:20.835 --> 01:05:22.327
You're loosing it.

581
01:05:23.179 --> 01:05:25.462
Pretty good. My dad said,

582
01:05:25.652 --> 01:05:29.005
as long as you still alive,
it's pretty good.

583
01:05:29.242 --> 01:05:30.553
Must I become the King?

584
01:05:30.644 --> 01:05:33.997
You'll be a good King.
It's a good thing for Wei.

585
01:05:34.054 --> 01:05:37.550
Are you trying to convince me
to kill him without a blink of an eye?

586
01:05:37.693 --> 01:05:40.999
We've gone this far,
this is only way out.

587
01:05:41.282 --> 01:05:44.179
Okay, how can he die

588
01:05:45.764 --> 01:05:47.720
with dignity?

589
01:05:48.886 --> 01:05:50.286
What are you thinking?

590
01:05:51.731 --> 01:05:53.082
Rapeseed flower.

591
01:05:55.787 --> 01:05:57.605
I'm thinking about growing rapeseed.

592
01:05:57.748 --> 01:05:58.821
Why?

593
01:05:59.010 --> 01:05:59.943
Why what?

594
01:06:00.134 --> 01:06:02.184
Why am I being stuck here?

595
01:06:03.547 --> 01:06:06.948
I should be the one who brings
all the Dukes to their knees.

596
01:06:07.183 --> 01:06:09.419
And then have a huge tomb
made for me.

597
01:06:09.610 --> 01:06:12.498
Have my own treasure
buried with me.

598
01:06:13.896 --> 01:06:15.853
Now they can't even
find my corpse.

599
01:06:17.066 --> 01:06:22.095
Yeah, the rest of reward money
would go to my new pharmacy store.

600
01:06:22.286 --> 01:06:24.800
To be honest, your drug worked.

601
01:06:25.874 --> 01:06:29.456
I'm appointing you as
The Minister for Health.

602
01:06:34.024 --> 01:06:38.522
You know what, if it wasn't the wars,
we could have been buddies.

603
01:06:39.242 --> 01:06:40.732
Perhaps.

604
01:06:42.271 --> 01:06:44.135
If you make it out alive,

605
01:06:44.743 --> 01:06:47.910
will you promise me one thing?

606
01:06:48.100 --> 01:06:49.312
Shoot.

607
01:06:51.455 --> 01:06:53.925
Never invade my nation.

608
01:07:02.722 --> 01:07:05.239
I give you 10 years of truce.

609
01:07:06.730 --> 01:07:09.851
Sounds tricky.
We have an agreement.

610
01:07:13.911 --> 01:07:15.775
And you need to promise me one thing.

611
01:07:15.876 --> 01:07:16.776
Shoot.

612
01:07:16.855 --> 01:07:18.672
If you ever make it out alive,

613
01:07:19.512 --> 01:07:21.376
you must tell them that

614
01:07:23.613 --> 01:07:24.964
I died fighting.

615
01:07:25.619 --> 01:07:28.459
I died fighting for my people.

616
01:07:29.346 --> 01:07:31.594
I've done nothing disgraceful
to Wei.

617
01:07:33.029 --> 01:07:38.523
We all bite the dust,
but not our flag.

618
01:07:40.899 --> 01:07:42.679
Don't lie to me,

619
01:07:43.519 --> 01:07:45.478
you small potato.

620
01:07:46.457 --> 01:07:48.400
Being a small potato...

621
01:07:48.957 --> 01:07:50.490
sounds pretty good.

622
01:09:33.137 --> 01:09:34.957
Wake up.

623
01:09:53.389 --> 01:09:57.301
Dad, I'm alive!

624
01:09:58.422 --> 01:10:00.332
Thanks Heaven!

625
01:10:00.754 --> 01:10:03.037
Thanks Heaven!

626
01:10:04.446 --> 01:10:07.240
You know what, this is
Three Legs Cave.

627
01:10:07.383 --> 01:10:09.725
There is a fisherman's village nearby.
I'll go get a boat.

628
01:10:10.008 --> 01:10:11.312
It'll take half a day to get there.

629
01:10:11.503 --> 01:10:12.901
To where?

630
01:10:13.091 --> 01:10:15.766
To Liang, where else could it be?

631
01:10:16.494 --> 01:10:20.999
Don't think about running away.
You can't survive an hour without me.

632
01:10:28.647 --> 01:10:29.999
Quick, quick!

633
01:10:30.885 --> 01:10:31.912
Go hide!

634
01:10:32.103 --> 01:10:33.222
Hide from what?

635
01:10:33.411 --> 01:10:34.856
Just hide.

636
01:10:37.139 --> 01:10:38.491
Hold me up.

637
01:10:46.128 --> 01:10:47.386
Brother.

638
01:10:48.320 --> 01:10:50.091
Brother?

639
01:10:51.443 --> 01:10:53.028
He's your brother?

640
01:10:53.172 --> 01:10:55.594
You've been chasing me for days.
Don't you get tired?

641
01:10:55.797 --> 01:10:56.683
Prince.

642
01:10:56.873 --> 01:10:58.039
Prince?

643
01:10:58.227 --> 01:10:59.674
Why the mourning bandana?

644
01:10:59.910 --> 01:11:01.401
It's for our father.

645
01:11:01.591 --> 01:11:04.479
He was very sick when I left for battles.
It's you.

646
01:11:04.631 --> 01:11:07.984
It's fate. You just cared about
waging wars to please the old man.

647
01:11:08.174 --> 01:11:11.123
If I hadn't upset him by making
peace arrangement with Liang,

648
01:11:11.292 --> 01:11:12.704
I would have been the Prince.

649
01:11:12.848 --> 01:11:15.363
You set the ambush to make sure
I'd get killed.

650
01:11:16.016 --> 01:11:17.567
Something going on between you two

651
01:11:17.757 --> 01:11:19.575
and we Liang paid with 2,000 lives.

652
01:11:19.764 --> 01:11:20.977
You're not authorized to talk to me.

653
01:11:21.166 --> 01:11:23.031
You're not authorized to talk to me.

654
01:11:24.302 --> 01:11:26.632
- Leave him out of this.
- But he's the enemy.

655
01:11:26.733 --> 01:11:28.603
He wants me to live,
but you wants me to die.

656
01:11:28.704 --> 01:11:33.514
Come on. Use that bow I gave you
and claim the throne of Wei.

657
01:11:40.105 --> 01:11:42.015
You're still too soft-hearted.

658
01:11:45.016 --> 01:11:46.516
Your sword.

659
01:11:46.617 --> 01:11:50.117
If you don't kill him, he will kill you.

660
01:11:51.018 --> 01:11:53.018
Only one of you will become the King.

661
01:11:56.219 --> 01:11:59.609
That's doesn't make any senses,
why one of you brothers must die?

662
01:11:59.710 --> 01:12:00.610
It's none of your business.

663
01:12:00.611 --> 01:12:02.911
You guys are complicating things.

664
01:12:02.912 --> 01:12:04.412
I said it's none of your business!

665
01:12:04.513 --> 01:12:07.313
It's all because of that nosy baldhead.

666
01:12:09.514 --> 01:12:10.514
I'm done talking.

667
01:12:23.115 --> 01:12:25.615
He really looks upset.
Maybe we should go now.

668
01:12:31.816 --> 01:12:33.316
I'm really messed up big time.

669
01:12:33.517 --> 01:12:36.317
You do what you got to do, Master.

670
01:12:57.418 --> 01:12:59.218
Can we go now?

671
01:14:20.696 --> 01:14:21.714
General!

672
01:14:22.215 --> 01:14:23.415
Behind you!

673
01:14:28.216 --> 01:14:29.416
It's none of my business.

674
01:14:34.717 --> 01:14:36.117
What a pity.

675
01:15:19.418 --> 01:15:20.918
Not even one small rock?

676
01:15:47.219 --> 01:15:48.719
Don't get any closer,

677
01:15:48.920 --> 01:15:50.320
or you'd get blind.

678
01:15:53.021 --> 01:15:54.321
<i>Big brother!</i>

679
01:16:58.714 --> 01:17:00.114
Stop!

680
01:17:03.405 --> 01:17:05.115
I'm the one you need to kill.

681
01:17:06.916 --> 01:17:08.916
I'm the one you need to kill.

682
01:17:10.117 --> 01:17:14.617
Me and my brother,
only one will walk out here alive.

683
01:17:16.606 --> 01:17:18.749
You don't understand
what I'm saying, do you?

684
01:17:23.810 --> 01:17:25.907
How about this?

685
01:17:26.389 --> 01:17:28.034
This is what I got to do.

686
01:17:28.394 --> 01:17:29.632
<i>Little brother!</i>

687
01:17:36.080 --> 01:17:37.287
Big brother,

688
01:17:38.080 --> 01:17:40.597
am I dying with dignity?

689
01:17:42.527 --> 01:17:46.467
Sorry about our big boat.

690
01:17:47.107 --> 01:17:50.568
We can never build it together.

691
01:18:36.608 --> 01:18:37.866
Do me a favor.

692
01:18:39.306 --> 01:18:41.044
Help me bury him.

693
01:18:46.492 --> 01:18:50.870
We must carry on, General.
We got half day.

694
01:18:51.758 --> 01:18:54.924
Sorry, I mean Prince.

695
01:19:00.279 --> 01:19:02.515
Your Wei's liquor is not strong enough.

696
01:19:04.706 --> 01:19:06.802
I know what you're thinking.

697
01:19:06.991 --> 01:19:08.530
I also know what you're thinking.

698
01:19:12.024 --> 01:19:15.657
- Pretty good.
- We're still alive.

699
01:19:17.799 --> 01:19:22.115
You two reminded me
of my own brothers.

700
01:19:22.379 --> 01:19:23.778
They were good soldiers.

701
01:19:23.968 --> 01:19:26.112
In fact, I wanted to be a good soldier.

702
01:19:27.510 --> 01:19:31.329
The first time we enlisted,
we 3 brothers got no choice.

703
01:19:31.565 --> 01:19:33.662
The first tour lasted for 3 years.

704
01:19:34.001 --> 01:19:35.493
When we came back,

705
01:19:36.427 --> 01:19:38.431
our village had been burnt to ground.

706
01:19:39.270 --> 01:19:40.622
We became homeless.

707
01:19:41.882 --> 01:19:43.803
Before my dad died, he told us

708
01:19:45.016 --> 01:19:47.346
we had served our country.

709
01:19:49.008 --> 01:19:53.432
But when the wars will end?

710
01:19:54.691 --> 01:19:59.207
And he said, "kids, listen,

711
01:20:02.143 --> 01:20:04.473
one of you 3 brothers must live,

712
01:20:09.036 --> 01:20:11.633
in order to raise kids for our family."

713
01:20:13.323 --> 01:20:16.071
Now I'm the only one left.

714
01:20:20.168 --> 01:20:24.871
Having you is my biggest luck ever.

715
01:20:32.786 --> 01:20:37.395
I can't say the same thing about my luck.

716
01:20:52.709 --> 01:20:54.061
Don't ask.

717
01:20:54.668 --> 01:20:56.906
What she said to me the other night:

718
01:20:58.536 --> 01:21:00.259
"kama".

719
01:21:02.523 --> 01:21:04.068
What a little potato.

720
01:21:13.901 --> 01:21:16.501
Shen Shu, Mt. Phoenix.

721
01:21:21.702 --> 01:21:27.403
"Peace"

722
01:21:41.871 --> 01:21:43.316
"Mt. Liang"

723
01:21:43.459 --> 01:21:46.886
You know what,
after this turn is Liang's soil.

724
01:21:51.655 --> 01:21:55.194
My brother wanted to befriend
Liang, maybe he's right.

725
01:21:55.348 --> 01:21:58.740
If Liang's Duke spare my life, may be we could
work something out for allying each other.

726
01:21:58.860 --> 01:22:00.352
Maybe, maybe.

727
01:22:02.318 --> 01:22:03.904
Maybe it's too late.

728
01:22:04.791 --> 01:22:06.281
Maybe.

729
01:22:20.945 --> 01:22:22.903
Nothing feels like home!

730
01:22:27.420 --> 01:22:28.770
That's your secret bet...

731
01:22:37.942 --> 01:22:39.674
I was wrong about you.

732
01:22:40.609 --> 01:22:43.663
Never thought you could make
this journey for both of us.

733
01:22:44.429 --> 01:22:47.793
Now, am I your captive or enemy?

734
01:22:54.775 --> 01:22:57.059
Neither. Just go.

735
01:22:59.527 --> 01:23:01.960
Hurry. Before I change my mind.

736
01:23:06.382 --> 01:23:07.689
Why?

737
01:23:08.948 --> 01:23:12.115
You 2 brothers, one must live.

738
01:23:23.068 --> 01:23:24.605
Can I count on your word?

739
01:23:25.129 --> 01:23:26.387
What you mean?

740
01:23:26.578 --> 01:23:28.301
10 years of truce!

741
01:23:28.493 --> 01:23:31.752
Absolutely! You have my word!

742
01:23:35.906 --> 01:23:37.445
Don't forget...

743
01:23:37.913 --> 01:23:41.099
that medal you took from me,
it's worth a fortunate.

744
01:23:41.408 --> 01:23:44.714
It can get your farmland and money.

745
01:23:46.253 --> 01:23:47.837
I found it.

746
01:23:50.586 --> 01:23:52.356
I might not live long enough...

747
01:23:54.507 --> 01:23:57.721
Now I'm empty-handed.
Pretty good.

748
01:24:01.305 --> 01:24:02.728
Run.

749
01:24:04.685 --> 01:24:06.177
Run away now.

750
01:24:45.787 --> 01:24:47.325
Ask him to surrender.

751
01:24:49.514 --> 01:24:52.264
Liang has been destroyed.
Knee down and surrender.

752
01:24:54.872 --> 01:24:56.456
Liang is gone?

753
01:24:57.623 --> 01:24:58.882
How could that possible?

754
01:24:59.071 --> 01:25:02.159
Liang refused to surrender.
So we, from Qin, destroyed it.

755
01:25:02.288 --> 01:25:05.827
- Your units have been completely eliminated.
- On your knee. Last chance.

756
01:25:05.970 --> 01:25:07.835
All units wiped out?

757
01:25:08.003 --> 01:25:09.559
No more Liang.

758
01:25:09.960 --> 01:25:11.160
"Qin"

759
01:25:11.296 --> 01:25:12.671
This is not happening.

760
01:25:33.001 --> 01:25:34.453
Liang is history.

761
01:25:36.961 --> 01:25:39.010
I really got nothing left now.

762
01:25:41.387 --> 01:25:43.849
Put the flag down.

763
01:25:50.187 --> 01:25:53.122
<i>One main road</i>

764
01:25:53.728 --> 01:25:55.178
Your units have been wiped out.

765
01:25:55.273 --> 01:25:56.394
That's not true.

766
01:25:58.306 --> 01:25:59.306
Drop your sword.

767
01:25:59.307 --> 01:26:01.264
I'm still standing!
Give your best shot!

768
01:26:01.359 --> 01:26:04.502
<i>My home is right at</i>

769
01:26:07.009 --> 01:26:09.322
<i>the foot of Mt. Liang</i>

770
01:26:10.725 --> 01:26:18.499
<i>Soils are rich there
5 acres of farms</i>

771
01:26:19.991 --> 01:26:22.426
<i>5 acres of farm</i>

772
01:26:22.570 --> 01:26:27.958
Dad, sorry I can't raise any kids now.

773
01:26:30.682 --> 01:26:34.402
<i>One big river
leads to my home</i>

774
01:26:35.202 --> 01:26:38.212
<i>leads to my home</i>

775
01:26:39.891 --> 01:26:46.735
<i>My wife, my kids
and my big house</i>

776
01:26:49.344 --> 01:26:53.606
<i>Chickens and ducks are fat</i>

777
01:26:54.204 --> 01:26:58.096
<i>Cattle is strong</i>

778
01:26:59.681 --> 01:27:03.024
<i>Grow some bean
white grain</i>

779
01:27:03.681 --> 01:27:07.224
<i>and rapeseed flower</i>

780
01:27:31.569 --> 01:27:34.210
I ain't a shame to Liang, am I?

781
01:27:37.211 --> 01:27:39.011
"Liang"

782
01:27:40.000 --> 01:27:45.800
Subtitles/translation: Arigon

783
01:27:46.233 --> 01:27:49.028
Qin conquered Liang.

784
01:27:49.402 --> 01:27:52.151
The General has returned to Wei
and claimed the throne.

785
01:27:52.480 --> 01:27:55.041
Since then he gave up waging wars.

786
01:27:55.278 --> 01:28:00.027
When facing the invasion of Qin,
Wei's Duke complied to surrender.

787
01:28:00.263 --> 01:28:03.570
Soldiers and civilians
were left to life in peace.

788
01:28:03.807 --> 01:28:06.406
During the last few years of
the Warring States Period,

789
01:28:06.507 --> 01:28:08.507
one China was nearly shaped.

790
01:28:08.680 --> 01:28:14.481
Qin united all states of China
in 221 B.C.
